WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.341 --> 00:00:01.195
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 1

2
00:00:01.991 --> 00:00:06.531
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> The busiest shopping street in Europe is Oxford Street.

3
00:00:06.748 --> 00:00:12.221
Although numbers dropped during the Covid-19 pandemic, seventy-two thousand

4
00:00:12.221 --> 00:00:16.898
shoppers a day still visit the street in the centre of London.

5
00:00:18.604 --> 00:00:19.412
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 2

6
00:00:20.175 --> 00:00:25.921
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> The biggest railway station in the world is Grand Central Terminal in New York.

7
00:00:26.205 --> 00:00:32.691
It has forty-four platforms, and covers nearly two hundred thousand square metres.

8
00:00:34.319 --> 00:00:35.616
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 3

9
00:00:36.185 --> 00:00:41.692
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> The tallest cathedral in the world is Ulm Münster in Germany.

10
00:00:41.851 --> 00:00:45.515
It is a hundred and sixty-one metres tall.

11
00:00:47.108 --> 00:00:48.155
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 4

12
00:00:48.792 --> 00:00:53.754
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> The oldest bridge in Europe is the Arkadiko Bridge in Greece.

13
00:00:53.913 --> 00:00:59.511
People still use it today. It was built more than three thousand years ago.

14
00:01:02.242 --> 00:01:03.448
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 5

15
00:01:03.926 --> 00:01:07.340
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> The longest river in the world is the Nile.

16
00:01:07.647 --> 00:01:11.448
It’s six thousand six hundred and fifty kilometres long

17
00:01:11.652 --> 00:01:15.169
and goes through eleven different African countries.

18
00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:18.355
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 6

19
00:01:18.901 --> 00:01:26.069
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> The most dangerous road in the world is Bayburt D-nine-one-five in Türkiye.

20
00:01:26.479 --> 00:01:33.580
The one hundred and six-kilometre road is very high up and the weather is often foggy and rainy.

21
00:01:33.739 --> 00:01:38.654
Even really good drivers find driving extremely difficult.